  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "Halving MGDA optimizer steps from 64 to 32 per 8,192 environment hands will move the 65,536-hand endpoint to the prior curve's preservation-safe 32k-equivalent optimizer dose while benefiting from twice the on-policy environment diversity, yielding positive 16k-to-65k holdout slopes in at least two of three seeds without source-boundary failure.",
  "material_change": "Repeat the exact six-train/three-holdout mixed-contract three-seed 65,536-hand protocol with the same seeds, chunk size, residual cap, group batch, frozen identities, evaluation doses/decks, and 512 pairs per holdout. Change only steps-per-chunk from 64 to 32. Preserve restart-safe chunk evidence and compare the resulting 65k endpoint to both its own 16k curve and the prior 64-step run's 32k optimizer-dose boundary.",
  "baseline": "The 64-step run had all-positive MGDA geometry but 32k-to-65k slopes negative in 3/3 seeds, cap saturation at 24k-32k, and a seed2 source failure. Its 32k dose passed all source/breadth gates with 2/3 positive 16k-to-32k slopes and median holdout/seat deltas +31.05/+26.86.",
